Subject: [PATCH 08005/11362] [outer-loop] HAZARD: running the test suite
 silently rewrites the research record

DIAGNOSED, NOT FIXED. No test was changed and no fix is shipped. This records a hazard found while
verifying the retention commit (111f5d331), so it is not lost.

Running `pytest tests/python/test_arc_*.py tests/python/test_experiment_*.py` left 39 tracked files
modified that were clean before the run -- 36 results/*.json and .log artifacts plus
openspec/papers/paper-v6/section-6-limitations.md and output/kanele_synth/post_synth.dcp. All 39
were reverted by hand and the three protected evidence directories verified byte-identical by
mtime+path digest afterwards.

The rewrites are never-prune violations, not cosmetic:
  * experiment_3946_r11l_first_solve.json LOST its inference_substrate_correction_note -- a
    hand-written 2026-07-27 corrigendum explaining why the original substrate string was illegal --
    along with its solve_provenance field.
  * experiment_307_jepa_real_training.json had inference_mode flipped live_gpu -> cpu_training.
  * experiment_1035_dualgpu_rocm_v3.json had run_date/started_at/finished_at rewritten to today.

MECHANISM: a class of test_experiment_*.py tests calls runpy.run_path on the real
scripts/experiments/experiment_NNNN_*.py and then asserts the artifact exists. The script writes
its artifact as a side effect, overwriting the historical record. 123 test files call
runpy.run_path; 11 target scripts/experiments/. The exact artifact-writing set was NOT enumerated --
the three above are confirmed instances, not a survey.

WHY IT MATTERS: these artifacts are the input to the fabrication gate, the adversarial verifier and
every capstone aggregation. A green test run that rewrites a run_date, flips an inference_mode, or
deletes a corrigendum makes the record disagree with what was measured, silently. Anyone who runs
the suite and commits with `git add -A` publishes those rewrites.

Not fixed here because the repair is a design call across 11+ call sites with an operator-visible
tradeoff (redirect the output dir / snapshot-and-restore / stop re-running the script and assert
against the committed artifact -- the last stops exercising the script at all).

