+## 2026-07-29 (outer-loop: HAZARD — running the test suite silently REWRITES the research record)
+
+TRIGGER: found while verifying the REQ-ARC-WMTE-6035 retention commit above. Recorded as a hazard;
+**no fix is shipped here** and no test was changed.
+
+### WHAT HAPPENED
+
+Running `pytest tests/python/test_arc_*.py tests/python/test_experiment_*.py` left **39 tracked
+files modified** that were clean before the run — 36 `results/*.json` and `.log` artifacts, plus
+`openspec/papers/paper-v6/section-6-limitations.md` and `output/kanele_synth/post_synth.dcp`. All 39
+were reverted by hand; the working tree and the three protected evidence directories
+(`results/arc_e3`, `results/arc_logo_snapshot`, `results/arc_e3_origin_fixtures`) were verified
+byte-identical afterwards by mtime+path digest.
+
+These were not cosmetic rewrites. Examples, each a violation of the never-prune rule:
+
+- `results/experiment_3946_r11l_first_solve.json` — **lost its `inference_substrate_correction_note`
+  entirely**, a hand-written 2026-07-27 corrigendum recording why the original substrate string was
+  illegal and what replaced it, together with its `solve_provenance: development_proxy` field. That
+  note exists precisely so a future reader is not misled about the artifact's provenance, and a test
+  run deleted it.
+- `results/experiment_307_jepa_real_training.json` — `inference_mode` flipped `live_gpu` ->
+  `cpu_training`, i.e. a claim about which hardware produced a historical result was silently
+  changed.
+- `results/experiment_1035_dualgpu_rocm_v3.json` — `run_date` / `started_at` / `finished_at`
+  rewritten from the real 2026-07-27 run to today.
+
+### THE MECHANISM
+
+A class of `test_experiment_*.py` tests RE-EXECUTES the real experiment script against the live repo:
+
+```python
+runpy.run_path(str(script_path), run_name="__main__")   # scripts/experiments/experiment_NNNN_*.py
+...
+assert result_path.exists()                              # results/experiment_NNNN_*.json
+```
+
+The script writes its artifact as a side effect, overwriting whatever the historical record held.
+123 test files call `runpy.run_path`; 11 of them target `scripts/experiments/`. The exact set that
+writes artifacts was NOT enumerated — the three above are confirmed instances, not a survey.
+
+### WHY IT MATTERS BEYOND THE LOST TEXT
+
+The artifacts are the project's measurement record and the input to the fabrication gate, the
+adversarial verifier, and every capstone aggregation. A test run that rewrites `run_date` to today,
+flips an `inference_mode`, or deletes a corrigendum makes the record disagree with what was actually
+measured — and it does so silently, with a green test suite. Anyone who runs the suite and then
+commits with `git add -A` publishes those rewrites.
+
+### NOT DONE HERE, DELIBERATELY
+
+No test was modified. Fixing this properly means deciding whether these tests should (a) run the
+script against a redirected output directory, (b) snapshot-and-restore the artifact, or (c) be
+replaced by assertions against the committed artifact without re-running anything — a design call
+with 11+ call sites and an operator-visible tradeoff (option (c) stops exercising the script at all).
+Interim guidance for anyone running the suite: check `git status` afterwards and revert unintended
+`results/` changes before committing.
